            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h='7210' id='8' type-v2='text' w='97538' x='1231' y='91860'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='8' italic='true'>Notes:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='8' italic='true'> This dataset is one row per claim (not per policy), so this ratio is a claims-cost-to-premium proxy for claiming policies — not a true book-wide loss ratio, which would require premium from non-claiming policies too. Dataset is a US-based synthetic tutorial dataset (Illinois, Indiana, Ohio only), not real company data.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h='9535' id='7' type-v2='text' w='97538' x='1231' y='45000'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Claim severity — not policy state — drives the claims-to-premium ratio.</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'> Ratio ranges from 4.3 (Trivial Damage) to 51.1 (Major Damage) across severity, versus a narrow 41.6–42.2 spread across the three states in this dataset.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
